<node id="Settimia Caccini">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An Italian singer and composer during the 1600s, known for her artistic and technical work with music.", "chunk_id": "95c365ca672cb565", "doc_id": "hp_854c21bf573c6370"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Settimia Caccini (6 October 1591 – ca. 1638, Italy) was a well-known Italian singer and composer during the 1600s being one of the first women to have a successful career in music.", "chunk_id": "95c365ca672cb565", "doc_id": "hp_854c21bf573c6370"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_854c21bf573c6370"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Giulio Caccini">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A famed composer of the time, known for helping to establish monodic music and being Settimia Caccini's father.", "chunk_id": "95c365ca672cb565", "doc_id": "hp_854c21bf573c6370"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "As well as her father being into music she also had an older sister who was a famous composer of the time. Although she is not as well known as her sister, Francesca Caccini, mostly due to the fact Settimia never published any of her own music composed pieces of music. Instead she was known much more for her talent as a singer, who sang for nobility across Italy. It is thought that she did compose her own music but instead of publishing and releasing it to be performed instead she kept it for herself for her to perform in private. One of her pieces eventually did get published once she had passed. Coming from a family full of talent her works are not as well known as her sister's compositions but nonetheless she was able to lead herself to her own fame and success.", "chunk_id": "95c365ca672cb565", "doc_id": "hp_854c21bf573c6370"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_854c21bf573c6370"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Francesca Caccini">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A famous composer of the time, known as Settimia Caccini's older sister.", "chunk_id": "95c365ca672cb565", "doc_id": "hp_854c21bf573c6370"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "As well as her father being into music she also had an older sister who was a famous composer of the time. Although she is not as well known as her sister, Francesca Caccini, mostly due to the fact Settimia never published any of her own music composed pieces of music.", "chunk_id": "95c365ca672cb565", "doc_id": "hp_854c21bf573c6370"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_854c21bf573c6370"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Monodic Music">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A type of music that opposed traditional music by having expressive melodies and evocative chords.", "chunk_id": "95c365ca672cb565", "doc_id": "hp_854c21bf573c6370"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "This type of music opposed traditional music then, by having expressive melodies and evocative chords.", "chunk_id": "95c365ca672cb565", "doc_id": "hp_854c21bf573c6370"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_854c21bf573c6370"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Italy">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The country where Settimia Caccini lived and had her career.", "chunk_id": "95c365ca672cb565", "doc_id": "hp_854c21bf573c6370"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Settimia Caccini (6 October 1591 – ca. 1638, Italy) was a well-known Italian singer and composer during the 1600s being one of the first women to have a successful career in music.", "chunk_id": "95c365ca672cb565", "doc_id": "hp_854c21bf573c6370"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_854c21bf573c6370"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
