<node id="Chandler Bing">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A character from the TV show 'Friends', known for his sarcasm and high earning status.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}, {"text": "A character from the NBC sitcom 'Friends', portrayed by Matthew Perry.", "chunk_id": "702e5a74aed1bc94", "doc_id": "hp_e8285dadbc32439e"}, {"text": "A character played by Matthew Perry in the sitcom 'Friends'.", "chunk_id": "8f5e44d5eaa0b180", "doc_id": "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Chandler Bing, a character from the TV show 'Friends', is known for his sarcasm and high earning status.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}, {"text": "his roommate and best friend, Chandler Bing", "chunk_id": "702e5a74aed1bc94", "doc_id": "hp_e8285dadbc32439e"}, {"text": "It featured six main cast members: Rachel Green (Jennifer Aniston), Phoebe Buffay (Lisa Kudrow), Joey Tribbiani (Matt LeBlanc), Chandler Bing (Matthew Perry)", "chunk_id": "8f5e44d5eaa0b180", "doc_id": "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5", "hp_e8285dadbc32439e", "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ross Geller">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A character from the TV show 'Friends', Ross is Chandler's best friend from college.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}, {"text": "A character from the NBC sitcom 'Friends', portrayed by David Schwimmer.", "chunk_id": "702e5a74aed1bc94", "doc_id": "hp_e8285dadbc32439e"}, {"text": "A fictional character from the NBC sitcom 'Friends', portrayed by David Schwimmer.", "chunk_id": "1d759448fd704b25", "doc_id": "hp_ebd15cd476a830f6"}, {"text": "A character played by David Schwimmer in the sitcom 'Friends'.", "chunk_id": "8f5e44d5eaa0b180", "doc_id": "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Chandler's best friend is Ross Geller from the college.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}, {"text": "hangs out in a tight-knit group of friends - Chandler Bing, Ross Geller", "chunk_id": "702e5a74aed1bc94", "doc_id": "hp_e8285dadbc32439e"}, {"text": "Dr. Ross Eustace Geller, Ph.D., is a fictional character from the NBC sitcom 'Friends', portrayed by David Schwimmer.", "chunk_id": "1d759448fd704b25", "doc_id": "hp_ebd15cd476a830f6"}, {"text": "It featured six main cast members: Rachel Green (Jennifer Aniston), Phoebe Buffay (Lisa Kudrow), Joey Tribbiani (Matt LeBlanc), Chandler Bing (Matthew Perry), Ross Geller (David Schwimmer)", "chunk_id": "8f5e44d5eaa0b180", "doc_id": "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5", "hp_e8285dadbc32439e", "hp_ebd15cd476a830f6", "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Monica Geller">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A character from the TV show 'Friends', Monica is Ross's sister who Chandler meets during Thanksgiving.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}, {"text": "A character played by Courteney Cox in the sitcom 'Friends'.", "chunk_id": "8f5e44d5eaa0b180", "doc_id": "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He met Ross's sister, Monica Geller, while celebrating Thanksgiving at Ross's House.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}, {"text": "It featured six main cast members: Rachel Green (Jennifer Aniston), Phoebe Buffay (Lisa Kudrow), Joey Tribbiani (Matt LeBlanc), Chandler Bing (Matthew Perry), Ross Geller (David Schwimmer) and Monica Geller (Courteney Cox)", "chunk_id": "8f5e44d5eaa0b180", "doc_id": "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5", "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Way/No Way">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A band that Chandler and Ross were in during college.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He and Ross were in a band named Way/No Way during college.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Phoebe Buffay">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A character from the TV show 'Friends', Phoebe meets Chandler through Monica.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}, {"text": "A character from the NBC sitcom 'Friends', portrayed by Lisa Kudrow.", "chunk_id": "702e5a74aed1bc94", "doc_id": "hp_e8285dadbc32439e"}, {"text": "A character played by Lisa Kudrow in the sitcom 'Friends'.", "chunk_id": "8f5e44d5eaa0b180", "doc_id": "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "At some point during this time, Joey Tribbiani moved in with him and they became the best friends throughout the journey. Chandler has a very good sense of humor, and is notoriously sarcastic. He is personally the highest earning member of his friends due to responsible income management, and learning the value of money from a young age. He suffers from the commitment issues but later on, he ended up marrying Monica. He is afraid of dogs. He meets Phoebe Buffay through her.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}, {"text": "hangs out in a tight-knit group of friends - Chandler Bing, Ross Geller, Monica Geller-Bing, Rachel Green and Phoebe Buffay", "chunk_id": "702e5a74aed1bc94", "doc_id": "hp_e8285dadbc32439e"}, {"text": "It featured six main cast members: Rachel Green (Jennifer Aniston), Phoebe Buffay (Lisa Kudrow)", "chunk_id": "8f5e44d5eaa0b180", "doc_id": "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5", "hp_e8285dadbc32439e", "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Joey Tribbiani">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A character from the TV show 'Friends', Joey moves in with Chandler and they become best friends.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}, {"text": "A fictional character from the NBC sitcoms 'Friends' and its spin-off 'Joey', portrayed by Matt LeBlanc.", "chunk_id": "702e5a74aed1bc94", "doc_id": "hp_e8285dadbc32439e"}, {"text": "A character played by Matt LeBlanc in the sitcom 'Friends'.", "chunk_id": "8f5e44d5eaa0b180", "doc_id": "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "At some point during this time, Joey Tribbiani moved in with him and they became the best friends throughout the journey.", "chunk_id": "b1a1a41853d278db", "doc_id": "hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5"}, {"text": "Joey Tribbiani, Joseph Francis 'Joey' Tribbiani, Jr. is a fictional character from the NBC sitcoms 'Friends' and its spin-off 'Joey', portrayed by Matt LeBlanc.", "chunk_id": "702e5a74aed1bc94", "doc_id": "hp_e8285dadbc32439e"}, {"text": "It featured six main cast members: Rachel Green (Jennifer Aniston), Phoebe Buffay (Lisa Kudrow), Joey Tribbiani (Matt LeBlanc)", "chunk_id": "8f5e44d5eaa0b180", "doc_id": "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_8eaeb16bb356f2c5", "hp_e8285dadbc32439e", "hp_fe2995b8c6a6f60f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The Ecstatic">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The 2009 fourth studio album by American rapper Mos Def.", "chunk_id": "f2f6bd8122079227", "doc_id": "hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Ecstatic is the 2009 fourth studio album by American rapper Mos Def.", "chunk_id": "f2f6bd8122079227", "doc_id": "hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Downtown Records">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The record label that Mos Def signed with for The Ecstatic.", "chunk_id": "f2f6bd8122079227", "doc_id": "hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Mos Def signed with Downtown Records and recorded 'The Ecstatic' primarily at the Record Plant in Los Angeles.", "chunk_id": "f2f6bd8122079227", "doc_id": "hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Record Plant">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The studio where Mos Def recorded The Ecstatic.", "chunk_id": "f2f6bd8122079227", "doc_id": "hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Mos Def signed with Downtown Records and recorded 'The Ecstatic' primarily at the Record Plant in Los Angeles.", "chunk_id": "f2f6bd8122079227", "doc_id": "hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Preservation">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "One of the producers who worked on The Ecstatic.", "chunk_id": "f2f6bd8122079227", "doc_id": "hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He worked with producers such as Preservation, Mr. Flash, Oh No, and Madlib, the latter two of whom reused instrumentals they had produced on Stones Throw Records.", "chunk_id": "f2f6bd8122079227", "doc_id": "hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_8f34b0e5a3d7884e"]</data>
